ry:0f721f7b16d963f1275243effc34bdf39b40f0d76ff25cb0eba9d5bfb8309aca</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-afghanistan-no-female-doctor-often-means-no-treatment-for-women/a-80047053--cac71a2a15bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-afghanistan-no-female-doctor-often-means-no-treatment-for-women/a-80047053?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Millions of women in Afghanistan, particularly pregnant women, are suffering under Taliban restrictions and are increasingly losing access to life-saving medical care.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Catalan separatist Puigdemont sets date for return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a088a2ad44a9dfd53f77d68db3d70f1655494ebe6007054f9549b77686d28faa</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T11:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-catalan-separatist-puigdemont-sets-date-for-return/a-80045846--614f1341601e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-catalan-separatist-puigdemont-sets-date-for-return/a-80045846?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Catalan leader Carles Puigdemont plans to return to Barcelona on December 12 after nearly a decade in exile. Spain's Supreme Court has dropped the criminal case against him, clearing the way for his return.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea expels Swiss envoy over sanctions on camp accused of indoctrinating Ukrainian children</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbc87067e0b3476e7add5cddd001ab73ca1f0dc400b88752951ab34b5131aa05</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-expels-swiss-envoy-over-sanctions-on-camp-accused-of-indoctrinating-ukrainian-children/a-80043648--1c076b22f29b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-expels-swiss-envoy-over-sanctions-on-camp-accused-of-indoctrinating-ukrainian-children/a-80043648?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea has ordered Switzerland to close its newly reopened diplomatic office. The dispute centers on Swiss sanctions against a camp accused of indoctrinating Ukrainian children from Russian-occupied territories.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australia, Solomon Islands sign sweeping pact seen as countering China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d7081017309319fceedfefda9ffea3f0da3d9d08f7ee4896e53429568a74c406</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-solomon-islands-sign-sweeping-pact-seen-as-countering-china/a-80043646--0c4f82f58208.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-solomon-islands-sign-sweeping-pact-seen-as-countering-china/a-80043646?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Australia will become the Solomon Islands' primary security partner, while the archipelago will reject any foreign power trying to "interfere" on its "sensitive" infrastructure.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Deepfakes and 'US abandons Taiwan' claims spread ahead of vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd8988e4151d615dbeddd3b5c719073d8d9f0cc5fb2923da938b48d55e4f7fe2</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-deepfakes-and-us-abandons-taiwan-claims-spread-ahead-of-vote/a-80004834--56b12ab42141.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-deepfakes-and-us-abandons-taiwan-claims-spread-ahead-of-vote/a-80004834?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of local elections, Taiwan is seeing a surge in AI-generated attacks on mayoral candidate Puma Shen, alongside disinformation portraying the US as abandoning the island.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Houthis claim attacks on Saudi refinery, financial district</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df61c8c4945cb599c87e499f65662cde1c3a82bf67be50f3c2eb139109bece7c</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/houthis-claim-attacks-on-saudi-refinery-financial-district/a-80043632--c6099b35575b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/houthis-claim-attacks-on-saudi-refinery-financial-district/a-80043632?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran-backed Yemeni Houthis say they carried out fresh retaliatory attacks in Saudi Arabia. A fire was reported at Ras Tanura oil refinery and Riyadh's financial district was attacked for the second time in a week.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Climate loss and damage fund exists, but the money doesn't</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6aed051fd6c34f12d90fe578a7f933d1ddc68aa4c2e91bce801be8b03582a7c</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/climate-loss-and-damage-fund-exists-but-the-money-doesn-t/a-80035620--dbacc66829c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/climate-loss-and-damage-fund-exists-but-the-money-doesn-t/a-80035620?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Climate-vulnerable countries fought for years to create a loss and damage fund. Four years on, demand far outstrips funding, pledges are scarce, and disaster-hit nations are still waiting for support.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women's football team take stand against domestic violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00bec807280cfb7b67c25a92b00418a63bb5f51c5ba55673599e73a96dcb3be4</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T09:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-s-football-team-take-stand-against-domestic-violence/a-70907974--84aba926a54f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-s-football-team-take-stand-against-domestic-violence/a-70907974?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's women's football team are to wear UN Women badges in games against Argentina and Peru, as domestic violence hits a record high in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>German auto workers on back foot as costs, competition bite</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e56f40914439f779ff019aa2856061f14bf46d5f79e838206699d0a40f74d6a7</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T08:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-auto-workers-on-back-foot-as-costs-competition-bite/a-80036111--50a0a19d14b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-auto-workers-on-back-foot-as-costs-competition-bite/a-80036111?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German auto workers profited during the industry's boom years, but are now increasingly being asked to trade past gains for future job security.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: 'We can no longer afford everything,' Merz says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddc4105c8ebe8a747994229bd994f0dcfa83d0ae88a0f0db06b6007742cd4e48</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T08:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-we-can-no-longer-afford-everything-merz-says/live-80042795--0bc2dba71ae9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-we-can-no-longer-afford-everything-merz-says/live-80042795?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German chancellor has warned tax revenue means a tighter budget for 2027 and beyond. Meanwhile, President Steinmeier is in Kenya for the final leg of his Africa tour. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
